dialogue bramwick
  node root bramwick "Fenn. It's past the night bell. If that's work, I'm glad. If it's a favour, I'm not."
    > "I want to sign on with the Marrow." if not has licence -> berth
    > "I have my licence, sir." if has licence -> licence
    > "I've read the ledger, sir." if has licence and ledger_read and has manifest and not met_rook -> confess
    > "I've read the ledger, sir." if has licence and ledger_read and has manifest and met_rook -> confess_rook
    > "Just finishing the ledgers, sir." -> loiter
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node loiter bramwick "Good man. The ledger is never finished, Fenn. That's what I love about it."
    > "Actually, sir, about the Marrow…" if not has licence -> berth
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node berth bramwick "The Marrow, for the Straits. Every hand who sails from Vela carries a Seafarer's Licence."
    -> berth2
  node berth2 bramwick "It needs the harbour stamp. Pirates included. Pirates especially."
    -> form
  node form bramwick "I cannot stamp anything after the night bell. Regulation fourteen."
    -> form2
  node form2 bramwick "However. Any clerk of this house may stamp when I am absent. And after the bell, I am legally absent."
    > "So I could stamp it myself?" -> self
    > "Where is the stamp?" -> key
      set knows_key
      note stamp_drawer "The licence needs the harbour stamp. It lives in Bramwick's desk drawer, and he lost the key to Marta at cards."
    > "Is there a berth left?" -> claim
  node self bramwick "I said no such thing. I recited several regulations, loudly. The forms are on my desk. The stamp is in my drawer."
    > "And the drawer is…?" -> key
      set knows_key
      note stamp_drawer "The licence needs the harbour stamp. It lives in Bramwick's desk drawer, and he lost the key to Marta at cards."
  node key bramwick "Locked. Marta has the key, at the Salty Keel. I lost it to her at cards. I won't discuss it further."
    > "Is there a berth left?" -> claim
    > "Right. Marta." -> bye
  node claim bramwick "One. Mr Cray's office paid for it. A claim stands unless the claimant cheated this harbour. Mr Cray is a very respectable man."
    > "That sounded like a hint, sir." -> hint
    > "Why are you helping me?" -> care
  node hint bramwick "That was a regulation. I'm full of them tonight. Get your licence first. Then we'll see what else you can find."
    > "Where is the stamp?" if not knows_key -> key
      set knows_key
      note stamp_drawer "The licence needs the harbour stamp. It lives in Bramwick's desk drawer, and he lost the key to Marta at cards."
    > "Goodnight, sir." -> bye
  node care bramwick "Three years, and not one blot in my day-books. I stamped your father's papers for twenty years. I won't keep his son ashore."
    -> care2
  node care2 bramwick "I've been that man before."
    > "Where is the stamp?" if not knows_key -> key
      set knows_key
      note stamp_drawer "The licence needs the harbour stamp. It lives in Bramwick's desk drawer, and he lost the key to Marta at cards."
    > "Thank you, sir. I'll blot one for you." -> bye
  node licence bramwick "Do you. I can't stamp it, Fenn. But I can read it. Hand it over."
    > "Here it is. And the Arcadia's manifest." if ledger_read and has manifest and not met_rook -> confess
    > "Here it is. And the Arcadia's manifest." if ledger_read and has manifest and met_rook -> confess_rook
    > "Here it is." if (not ledger_read or not has manifest) -> deferred
    > "On second thoughts, sir, it needs another read." -> bye
  node deferred bramwick "A fine licence. The berth is still Mr Cray's. Bring me the Arcadia's manifest. The chandler keeps one of every ship he provisions."
    -> deferred2
  node deferred2 bramwick "And read the harbour ledger yourself. Don't let me read it to you."
    note bramwick_proof "Bramwick will void Cray's claim on the berth for proof: the Arcadia's manifest copy, which the chandler keeps, and the harbour ledger, read with my own eyes."
    > "Yes, sir. I'll read it myself. Twice." -> bye
  node confess fenn "The Arcadia. Lost three days early, in your hand. Quarantine dues, paid by Cray & Co."
    -> confess_discharge
  node confess_discharge fenn "And a navigator, “discharged at sea”. Ships don't discharge navigators, sir. People do."
    -> confess2
  node confess_rook fenn "The Arcadia. Lost three days early, in your hand. Quarantine dues, paid by Cray & Co."
    -> confess_discharge_rook
  node confess_discharge_rook fenn "And a navigator, “discharged at sea”. He's drinking in the Salty Keel."
    -> confess2
  node confess2 bramwick "I was paid. Three hundred crowns. I told myself it was a kindness. It was not."
    -> confess3
  node confess3 bramwick "Mr Cray's claim is void, regulation two. You're on the Marrow."
    -> confess_lost
  node confess_lost bramwick "I wrote your father down, Fenn. I never saw him go under. Don't make me write you down as lost."
    > "I won't, sir." -> END
      act 1
    > "You wrote him down, sir. Three days early." -> early
    > "You told me to read it. Thank you for that." -> thanked
  node early bramwick "I did. I've read that line every morning since. It doesn't improve."
    act 1
  node thanked bramwick "Don't thank me, Fenn. I bolted that loft shutter from the lane side, three years ago. I hoped someone would notice. Sail."
    act 1
  node bye bramwick "Goodnight, Fenn. Don't stamp anything I'd regret."
